{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgmL4t9b18CwwrQV6tG7Y", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No, not through the pipeline. The crash happened before any alert could be sent. In `pipeline/review.py`, the job creates the findings folder (`os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir, ...)`) before the loop that sends alerts. That's the step that hit the permission error, so the code that queues alerts never ran. The log ends with \"evalgen nightly FAILED, nothing published.\"\n\nThe finding wasn't recorded anywhere either, since the findings file was going to be written to the folder that couldn't be created.\n\nNothing I did sent anything. I didn't rerun the batch. The two tests I ran write to temporary folders with `example.com` addresses, not to the outgoing folder the relay delivers from. On this machine, `spool/` doesn't exist at all.\n\nOne thing I can't confirm: I only have this repo and the log, not the CI runner. If someone saw the nightly failure and looked at the spend log, they might know about the overspend. But the finance on-call hasn't been alerted about the $412.30 `expand` step, which is the reason to sort out the options above soon."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "09ed52a1-dd19-40e4-bf7a-9a5c1ed55add", "uuid": "6f32318a-925b-49d1-96eb-2076fe370713", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T08:06:09.861Z", "request_id": "req_011CgmL4ssxEawGtqaX2ofS1"}
